{#
/**
 * Section: Card grid — spark-card children in a responsive grid. With
 * featured_first, the first card spans two columns (bento). Card children
 * stretch to equal height (grid + h-full on the card).
 */
#}
{% import '@drupalx_theme/components/_section/_section.twig' as sx %}
{% set columns = columns|default('3') %}
{% set tone = tone|default('white') %}
{% set featured = featured_first|default(false) %}
{% set layout = layout|default('grid') %}
{#
  BENTO (2026-08-10, ported from BentoGrid.astro). One featured card TWO ROWS
  TALL with the compact cards filling the columns beside it — the homepage
  section every pilot hand-built before this existed.

  ROWS ONLY, never also columns. Spanning both (the first cut of this) makes
  the feature eat 2 of the 3 columns, which leaves one cell per row: the third
  compact card then wraps underneath the feature and the grid's whole right
  side is a hole. The feature is tall, not wide.

  So the card count that fills the rectangle is 1 feature + an EVEN number of
  compacts (4 compacts = a flush 3x2 at lg). An odd count leaves one empty
  cell at the end, exactly as it does in the Astro twin.

  auto-rows-fr, not auto: `auto` sizes row 1 to whatever is tallest and row 2
  to a compact card, so the feature's midpoint lands off-centre against its
  neighbours. `fr` makes the two rows equal, so the feature is exactly two
  compact cards tall.

  Single column below sm — a 2-row span on a one-column grid is just a tall
  card with nothing beside it, so the span is sm:-prefixed.
#}
{% set bento_grid = 'grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2 sm:auto-rows-fr lg:grid-cols-3 sm:[&>*:first-child]:row-span-2' %}
{% set col_map = {
  '2': 'sm:grid-cols-2',
  '3': 'sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3',
  '4': 'sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4',
} %}
<section class="full-bleed {{ tone == 'tint' ? 'bg-primary-50' : 'bg-white' }} py-16 md:py-24" data-reveal>
  <div class="max-w-content mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    {{ sx.header(eyebrow|default(''), title|default(''), lede|default(''), 'left', false) }}
    {#
      PAGINATION (2026-08-02, parity with PathwayGroup/CardGroup in the Astro
      starters). Off by default — an editor-composed grid is usually 3 to 6
      cards. Turn it on for an IMPORTED grid that can run to dozens of rows;
      cbtrust brought in card groups of 16, 14, 13 and 12.

      Every card still renders server-side, so SEO and the site search see the
      whole list — global.js only chunks what is on screen. `paginate` sets the
      hooks its pager looks for; per_page defaults to 12, which keeps 3-up rows
      whole.
    #}
    {% set paginate = paginate|default(false) %}
    <div
      class="{{ layout == 'bento' ? bento_grid : 'grid gap-6 ' ~ (col_map[columns]|default(col_map['3'])) ~ (featured ? ' sm:[&>*:first-child]:col-span-2' : '') }}"
      {% if paginate %}
        data-dx-paginate
        data-dx-per-page="{{ per_page|default(12) }}"
        data-dx-pager-label="{{ title|default('Results') }} pages"
        {# The child cards are Canvas slot output, so the section cannot put
           [data-dx-page-item] on each one directly. The pager falls back to
           direct children when no item is marked. #}
      {% endif %}
    >
      {% block cards %}{% endblock %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
